> Basically you seem to have:
> 
> peaceful music (sleep/pacify/taming)
> military music (berserk/haste pets)
> scary music

Also, you could have many songs, but you need to know the right tune
(offensive/defensive/taming) to play for each monster type. Undeads
like funeral music, snakes like flutes, each creature has a type from
its mythology. So if you're surrounded by bees you can use a buzzing
song to tame them, but if you're surrounded by both bees and manes,
you better run. Maybe you learn each song by listening to them, or
talking to peaceful creatures. You might get a special oracle, or run
into other bards that can teach you songs for different creatures.
Some of the more powerful songs require a music-playing pet to
accompany you. You quest artifact would be an instrument and score for
the E-word song. you could have a hundred different song, so a normal
bard couldn't find all of them in a single game.

I'd say music could be made powerful, but very specific and never 100
percent effective. So at any point the bard would have to choose
whether to cast a normal spell or play music.

